# .githooks/lib/credential-read-patterns.txt — glob patterns for files an
# agent should never read into context (credential/secret files). Consumed by
# .githooks/lib/agent-precheck when answering Cursor's beforeReadFile hook —
# the Cursor sibling of Claude Code's native `permissions.deny` credential
# list in claude-settings.json.template. Lives here, not under
# .forbidden-patterns/, because that directory is check-patterns' commit-time
# CONTENT-regex domain (a scaffold-extensions header selects which file
# extensions to scan) — these are PATH globs, a different contract, and
# putting them there would make check-patterns skip the file with a warning
# on every commit.
#
# Format: <glob><TAB><description>   (one per line; # comments ignored). A
# glob matches a read path exactly, or as a path suffix ("*/<glob>") — so
# ".ssh/*" matches both a relative ".ssh/config" and "/home/x/.ssh/config".
# Installed as `.githooks/lib/credential-read-patterns.txt`, by hand or
# by `install.sh --cursor` (cp_pattern: re-running install notifies on
# drift rather than overwriting your edits).

.env	environment file (secrets)
.env.*	environment file variant (secrets)
*.pem	PEM private key / certificate
*.key	private key file
id_rsa	SSH private key
id_ed25519	SSH private key
id_ecdsa	SSH private key
id_dsa	SSH private key
credentials	credentials file
.ssh/*	SSH keys/config directory
.aws/*	AWS credentials/config directory
.config/gcloud/*	gcloud credentials directory
.kube/config	Kubernetes config (cluster credentials)
.netrc	network credentials file
.npmrc	npm auth token file
